      "Saint John Chrysostom": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar honors Saint John Chrysostom on November 13. Born around 347 in Antioch and raised by his widowed mother Anthusa, John became a priest whose preaching was so clear and fervent that people called him golden-mouthed - Chrysostom. As archbishop of Constantinople he spoke for the poor and called the Church to conversion, which cost him exile; the Divine Liturgy prayed around the world still carries his name, and the Church honors him as a Doctor.": 1,
      "Brief story based on the Orthodox Church in America. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 2,
      "Read about Saint John Chrysostom": 1,
      "13.11.2026": 1,
      "J": 1,
      "13 Nov": 1,
      "Saint Philip the Apostle": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Philip the Apostle on November 14. Philip came from Bethsaida in Galilee, the town of Peter and Andrew. When Jesus called him with the words \"Follow me,\" Philip's first response was to find Nathanael and bring him to Christ with the invitation \"Come and see\" (John 1:43-46). One of the Twelve, he is remembered in tradition as a tireless preacher of the Gospel.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Philip the Apostle": 1,
      "14.11.2026": 1,
