      "14 Nov": 1,
      "Maronite commemoration; Sunday of the Announcement to Zechariah": 1,
      "Saints Gurias, Samonas and Habib": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saints Gurias, Samonas and Habib on November 15. Gurias and Samonas were Christians of Edessa who refused to abandon their faith during persecution. Habib, a deacon of the same city, bore witness to Christ in a later persecution. The Church remembers these martyrs together for their steadfast faith.": 1,
      "Brief account based on Orthodox Church in America. The date follows the Maronite calendar. This date is also the Sunday of the Announcement to Zechariah.": 1,
      "Read about Saints Gurias, Samonas and Habib": 1,
      "15.11.2026": 1,
      "S": 1,
      "15 Nov": 1,
      "Saint Matthew the Evangelist": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar honors Saint Matthew the Evangelist on November 16. The Gospel tells how Jesus called Matthew from his work as a tax collector, and Matthew rose and followed him. One of the Twelve Apostles, he is traditionally associated with the first Gospel. His call reminds Christians that the mercy of Christ opens the way to a new life.": 1,
      "Brief account based on Pope Benedict XVI's general audience of August 30, 2006, reproduced by EWTN. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Matthew the Evangelist": 1,
      "16.11.2026": 1,
