      "16 Nov": 1,
      "Saint Gregory the Wonderworker": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Gregory the Wonderworker on November 17. Born into a non-Christian family, Gregory encountered the Christian teacher Origen, studied with him and received baptism. He later became bishop of Neocaesarea, preaching the Gospel and guiding his community through persecution. The title Wonderworker reflects the miracles attributed to him in Christian tradition.": 1,
      "Brief account based on Vatican News. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Gregory the Wonderworker": 1,
      "17.11.2026": 1,
      "G": 1,
      "17 Nov": 1,
      "Saint Romanos the Martyr": 1,
      "The Maronite calendar remembers Saint Romanos on November 18. A deacon from Caesarea in Palestine, Romanos was living in Antioch when Christians faced persecution. He encouraged the faithful to remain steadfast and publicly confessed his faith in Christ. Arrested and imprisoned, he suffered martyrdom rather than deny that faith.": 1,
      "Brief account based on Orthodox Church in America. The date follows the Maronite calendar.": 1,
      "Read about Saint Romanos the Martyr": 1,
      "18.11.2026": 1,
